# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this file the checked-out form depends on
# each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, which makes a local `biome check` fail on
# Windows while CI (Linux) passes — a confusing, platform-specific false alarm.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository and lets git convert on
# checkout. The explicit `eol=lf` entries are for files where a conversion
# would change behaviour rather than just bytes.
* text=auto

# Shell and Node scripts must stay LF even on Windows: a CRLF shebang line
# produces `bad interpreter` when the script is executed.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Fixtures are exact input for tests. Normalising them would change what the
# parser is tested against, so they are stored and checked out byte-for-byte.
tests/fixtures/** -text
*.html -text

# Binary artefacts.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
